          "text": "Police can smell weed. People who use Fent aren't exactly cruising around in their cars bumping music while smoking a J. Many more people use weed than fent. Most cops who bust someone with fent are only catching an addict. But most weed people get arrested for sales because anything over a small amount is (in their world), sales. So.. little lesson here. Weed equals easy arrests. Fent, not so much. Think of it like this: if it was you.. would you wanna search, cuff and transport a fent addict.. consider all the logistics.. or would you be more apt to bust a Mom smoking weed with her kids in the car and she's got 3 oz on her? Since most cops don't smoke.. its an easy answer. The fent user is wild, sketchy, and what they have can literally kill you.. the weed smoker is calm, clean, and an easy arrest. Cops get performance reviews based on arrests. Fent users typically get released without prosecution. Simply because it's understood that they have almost zero choice or chance. And they make for horrible inmates. High costs to take care of, etc.. This is why. It has nothing to do with Big Pharma. Nothing at all."
